---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {Image} from 'astro:assets';
import MatterStory from './MatterStory.astro';
import VentureIndex from './VentureIndex.astro';
import ContactInvitation from './ContactInvitation.astro';
import ConnectionsExplorer from './ConnectionsExplorer.astro';
import IndustryDirectory from './IndustryDirectory.astro';
import QualityPlate from './QualityPlate.astro';
import JournalCard from './JournalCard.astro';
import '../styles/home-quality.css';
import architecture from '../assets/matterfield/matter-architecture.png';
import {getArticles} from '../data/content';
interface Props {draft?:boolean;}
const {draft=false}=Astro.props;
const articles=await getArticles(draft);
---
<Layout noindex={draft} description='NRTH Inc. is an independent company with nine venture directions across mobility, health, systems, materials, events and research. Build beyond.'>
 {draft&&<aside class='preview-banner'><a href='/preview'>Editorial workspace</a><span data-preview-status>Draft preview</span></aside>}
 <MatterStory draft={draft}/>
 <section class='portfolio-section' id='ventures'><div class='section-heading' data-enter><h2>Pick a<br/><em>possibility.</em></h2><p>NRTH brings nine venture directions together across technology, industry and experiences. Choose a field, find a venture and look inside the work.</p></div><VentureIndex filters draft={draft}/><div class='portfolio-reading-note'><p>Start with the audience, follow a workflow, then try a real-world scenario. Each overview separates the idea from the scope to discuss with NRTH.</p><a class='inline-link' href='/approach'>How we approach an idea</a></div></section>
 <section class='manifesto-section'><div class='manifesto-statement' data-enter><span class='section-label'>The company</span><h2>We see potential<br/>in the spaces<br/><em>between.</em></h2></div><div class='manifesto-image' data-image-reveal><Image src={architecture} alt='Conceptual graphite architecture with a warm orange aperture' widths={[640,1100,1600]} sizes='(max-width:767px) 100vw, 62vw' format='webp' loading='lazy'/><p class='manifesto-art-note'>A shared structure.<br/>Room for a different perspective.</p></div><div class='manifesto-copy' data-enter><p>A transportation plan needs trustworthy signals. A useful health interface needs a clear system. A material question needs the right experiment. A field can be distinct without standing alone.</p><p>NRTH is the company behind these venture directions. The portfolio gives each question a recognizable home, while leaving room to examine the connections around it.</p><div class='home-disclosures'><details><summary>What stays distinct?</summary><p>The audience, the problem and the evidence needed to move forward. A health information question and an industrial application need different expertise and review.</p></details><details><summary>What can travel?</summary><p>Methods for understanding workflows, designing interfaces and examining assumptions. A useful lesson can inform another direction without assuming its products or requirements are interchangeable.</p></details></div><a class='inline-link' href='/about'>Meet the company</a></div></section>
 <ConnectionsExplorer/>
 <IndustryDirectory draft={draft}/>
 <section class='research-spread'><div class='home-research-art'><QualityPlate kind='research' variant='nrth-labs' label='A question branches into different ways to learn.'/><div class='home-research-observation'><span>A smaller question</span><p>Where does an operational handoff lose its meaning?</p><span>A useful observation</span><p>What the receiving person can explain without filling in the gaps.</p></div></div><div class='research-spread-copy' data-enter><span class='section-label'>NRTH Labs</span><h2>The interesting<br/>part is<br/><em>what if.</em></h2><p>A question becomes more useful when its answer can change a decision. Research begins by making that connection explicit.</p><p>Explore six spatial studies, shape a bounded experiment and take away an outline with the inputs, observation and limits of the method you choose.</p><div class='home-research-links'><a class='inline-link' href='/research'>Enter the research</a><a href='/research#experiment'>Frame your own question</a><a href='/work'>See the design studies</a></div></div></section>
 <section class='journal-section'><div class='section-heading' data-enter><h2>Thinking<br/>out loud.</h2><p>Ideas you can put to work. Read a perspective, examine its example and take the questions back to your own context.</p></div><div class='home-journal-grid'>{articles.slice(0,3).map(article=><JournalCard article={article}/>)}</div><a class='inline-link home-journal-link' href='/insights'>Explore the journal</a></section>
 <section class='investor-bridge' data-enter><span class='section-label'>Investors</span><h2>A wider lens.<br/>A longer view.</h2><div><p>The portfolio is a starting point for inquiry. The meaningful details sit within each venture: who it concerns, what needs to be learned and which dependencies shape its next step.</p><div class='home-investor-reading'><a href='/investors#investor-comparison'><strong>Build a perspective</strong><span>Compare up to three venture directions across the same questions.</span></a><a href='/resources/nrth-company-overview.pdf' download><strong>Keep the context</strong><span>Save the company overview alongside your selected reading pack.</span></a><a href='/contact?project=investor'><strong>Ask for the specifics</strong><span>Discuss current stage, scope and the information relevant to your review.</span></a></div><a class='inline-link' href='/investors'>Investor conversations</a></div></section>
 <ContactInvitation/>
</Layout>
